      "response": {
        "type": "ai",
        "content": "HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol) is the foundation protocol for data exchange on the web. It defines how clients (like browsers) request resources from servers and how servers respond.\n\nKey points:\n- **Request/response model**: Client sends a request (e.g., GET /page), server returns a response (status code + content).\n- **Stateless**: Each request is independent; no built-in memory of previous requests.\n- **Common methods**: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE.\n- **Status codes**: 2xx success, 3xx redirect, 4xx client error, 5xx server error.\n- **Runs over TCP**, typically port 80 (HTTPS uses port 443 with TLS encryption).",
